WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
(whistle)

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:04.920
- Football is the most
popular sport in Sierra Leone.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.087
And in the city of Freetown,
there is one very special team.

00:00:09.357 --> 00:00:11.190
Meet the Flying Stars.

00:00:28.687 --> 00:00:30.963
Mohamed grew up playing football.

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:33.939
But when he was only 10 years
old he stepped on a landmine

00:00:33.939 --> 00:00:36.822
and had to have his right leg amputated.

00:00:36.822 --> 00:00:40.072
And unfortunately, Mohamed isn't alone.

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:50.924
Every member of the Flying
Stars has lost limbs

00:00:50.924 --> 00:00:53.070
as a result of the violence that occurred

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:56.301
during the Civil War in Sierra Leone.

00:00:56.301 --> 00:00:58.477
But the players don't let their injuries

00:00:58.477 --> 00:01:01.560
stop them from getting into the game.

00:01:59.275 --> 00:02:01.056
Not only is it a competitive sport,

00:02:01.056 --> 00:02:02.741
it is helping them cope
with their injuries

00:02:02.741 --> 00:02:04.354
and overcome the stigma

00:02:04.354 --> 00:02:07.354
that's associated with the disabled.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.623
And what better way than football.

